<title>GREECE: MACEDONIA-THRACE BANK TO ISSUE BONUS SHARES.</title>
<headline>MACEDONIA-THRACE BANK TO ISSUE BONUS SHARES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's Macedonia-Thrace Bank</p>
<p>plans to propose a one-for-five bonus issue to its</p>
<p>shareholders at the forthcoming annual general meeting, it said</p>
<p>on Thursday.</p>
<p>The bonus distribution is the result of a capitalisation of</p>
<p>reserves.</p>
<p>Its board will post extraordinary provisions for fiscal 1996</p>
<p>to improve the bank's asset base. This, however, will eliminate</p>
<p>its profit for the year.</p>
<p>&quot;The board has decided to propose to the shareholders'</p>
<p>general assembly the use of fiscal 1996 profit, which amounted</p>
<p>to 2.4 billion drachmas, for posting additional provisions to</p>
<p>cleanse the bank's balance sheet.&quot; the bank said.</p>
<p>Macedonia Thrace Bank's deposits, loans and assets in 1996</p>
<p>were as follows:</p>
<p>		     (drs bln)		 year/year</p>
<p>						    change</p>
<p>Deposits	  322.9			 +27.68pct</p>
<p>Loans	     205.4			 +26.56pct</p>
<p>Assets	    420.5			 +32.40pct</p>
<p>Equity	     24.1			 +50.60pct</p>
<p>--Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
